    <string-array name="monstera_facts">
        <item>Monstera deliciosa is famous for its natural leaf holes, which are called fenestrations.</item>
        <item>The fenestrations help the plant pass strong winds through without tearing the leaves in tropical rainforests.</item>
        <item>In its native habitat, it produces a delicious fruit that tastes like a mix of pineapple, banana, and mango.</item>
    </string-array>
